From 14649efc547d490ece28b787eb4043e130f6f440 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Waschkeit <44188360+HarryWaschkeit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 10:59:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] net: fec: defer probe instead of failing on netdev name
 collision

fec_probe() forces a fixed interface name (e.g. "eth0") via the
'ethernet0' OF alias before calling register_netdev(). If another
netdev has already registered with that literal name (e.g. an
on-board PCIe NIC that won the boot-time race against FEC's own
deferred probe retry), register_netdev() fails with -EEXIST and
fec_probe() currently treats this as a permanent, non-recoverable
error.

Since -EEXIST is not automatically retried by the deferred probe
core (only -EPROBE_DEFER is), this results in the FEC interface
never coming up for the rest of that boot, matching reports of
sporadic Ethernet probe failures after power-up on phyGATE-Tauri-L
boards that also have a fixed on-board PCIe NIC (igb) contending
for the same alias-derived name.

Convert the -EEXIST case into -EPROBE_DEFER so FEC re-joins the
deferred probe list and gets retried the next time any driver in
the system successfully binds, giving it further chances to claim
its fixed name once it frees up (e.g. once the competing interface
is renamed away by udev/systemd-networkd).

Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Harry Waschkeit <44188360+HarryWaschkeit@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c
index 33c58e9dd5e4..ea46d010f4f2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c
@@ -4559,8 +4559,21 @@ fec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		sprintf(ndev->name, "eth%d", eth_id);
 
 	ret = register_netdev(ndev);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		/*
+		 * If the OF alias forced this interface to a fixed name
+		 * (e.g. "eth0" via the 'ethernet0' alias) and that name is
+		 * already taken by another netdev that registered first
+		 * (e.g. an on-board PCIe NIC probed before us), defer our
+		 * probe instead of failing permanently. We'll get retried
+		 * automatically the next time any driver in the system
+		 * binds successfully, giving us another chance to claim
+		 * our fixed name once it becomes free.
+		 */
+		if (ret == -EEXIST && eth_id >= 0)
+			ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
 		goto failed_register;
+	}
 
 	device_init_wakeup(&ndev->dev, fep->wol_flag &
 			   FEC_WOL_HAS_MAGIC_PACKET);
